      "message": "feat(post): per-operation coolant - off, flood, mist or through tool\n\nEach operation now carries a coolant choice (Operation.coolant, the post\ncrate's CoolantMode), default Flood - what every built-in post already\nswitched on per section - so all CL/NC goldens stay byte-exact.\n\n- Stream: flood is the silent default; any other choice rides one\n  PARAM Coolant off|mist|through-tool ahead of the section.\n- Posts (Fanuc, Haas, Siemens 840D, Heidenhain, Mazak, Fanuc Lathe):\n  coolantFor() takes the mounted machine's own code for the family\n  (Flood / Mist / Through-spindle or Through-tool); M9 still closes\n  every section before M5, so coolant is off across tool changes and\n  at program end; a dry section writes neither word. A choice the\n  machine states no code for is a counted message() - the gate blocks\n  the post by name instead of cutting dry.\n- Command: EditOperationParams::with_coolant, one undo unit; the stamp\n  survives (coolant shapes no geometry).\n- UI: a Coolant row under Tool in the op page header grid\n  (CommandKind::EditOperationCoolant).\n- Project file: \"coolant\" written only off the default; absent reads\n  Flood, so older files load and round-trip unchanged.\n- Shell snapshots (egui_app.png / egui_app_light.png) updated: the op\n  page gains the Coolant row.\n\nFixes #112\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
